# patch: 002-claudiverse-sidecar-chunked
# format: CHUNKED ONLY (2.1.242+). Monolithic trees keep using
#         002-claudiverse-sidecar.patch, which is unchanged.
# version: authored against 2.1.260
# depends: 001
# description: Sidecar hooks for structuredIO and query mirroring.
#              prependUserMessage registers the StructuredIO instance; the query
#              entrypoint mirrors each inner-loop message to __claudiverse while
#              PRESERVING the loop's return value (the terminal `d`, consumed by
#              the downstream reason handling). After a top-level turn drains
#              (agentId absent, i.e. not a subagent) it emits a synthetic
#              {type:"turn_complete"} marker.
#
# LOAD-BEARING SHAPE (do not "simplify") — carried over verbatim from the
# monolithic patch, because the hazard is unchanged:
#     The manual-iteration rewrite `while (!(__s = await __it.next()).done)` is
#     deliberate. An earlier `for await (...) { yield ... }` attempt BROKE the
#     generator protocol: the delegated return value was lost, so the terminal
#     value came back undefined and the downstream reason handling faulted.
#     Manual iteration is the only shape that both taps every yielded value and
#     preserves `__s.value` on done. The ternary over the two loop generators is
#     preserved verbatim as the iterator initializer.
#
# WHERE THE CODE MOVED (chunked format):
#     query.js DOES NOT EXIST. bun's bundler merged the query driver into
#     services/compact/precomputedCompact.js — a 9.1 MB chunk named after one of
#     its many constituents. The hunk lands at ~line 182300 of that file.
#     cli/structuredIO.js survived under its own name.
#
# 🔴 MINIFIED NAMES ON CONTEXT LINES — UNAVOIDABLE, AND MITIGATED.
#     The `query` anchor chain does not resolve on chunked trees, so the
#     entrypoint is `EM` on 2.1.260 (MEASURED: it is `aN` on 2.1.259, and the
#     loop generators/notifier differ too — Rae/Y4o/I6n/Fue here vs
#     Yce/C5o/$qn/ope there). This patch is therefore version-locked and a bump
#     WILL require re-authoring; that is a property of the tree, not a shortcut.
#     ⚠️ NOTE the tree's own _renames.json maps "EM" -> "notifySubagentLifecycle",
#     which is WRONG — EM is the query entrypoint and the lifecycle notifier is
#     Fue. The mapping is inert (it is not applied to this chunk), but it is a
#     standing trap for anyone who trusts that file instead of reading the code.
#
#     Mitigation: every minified name sits in CONTEXT or on the REPLACED line;
#     the only names introduced on added lines are globalThis.__claudiverse and
#     the __-prefixed locals. So a rename of the entrypoint, its parameter or
#     the loop generators makes this FAIL TO APPLY rather than
#     apply-and-silently-stop-mirroring.
#     (The old header claimed a -U10 emission; that is no longer accurate — see
#      the 2026-09-07 note below for the context widths actually used.)
#
# WHY globalThis: see 001. The custom module's `var` is module-scoped in an ESM
# graph and would be silently undefined at these try-guarded call sites.
#
# ============================================================================
# RE-AUTHORED 2026-09-07 — RE-CONTEXTED TO 2.1.263
# ============================================================================
# STATUS: 🔴 VERSION-LOCKED. Applies to 2.1.263 ONLY (verified); FAILS on
#         2.1.260 (verified). This patch could NOT be made version-independent
#         and the blocking symbols are named below rather than papered over.
#
# WHAT BLOCKS IT — hunk 2, the generator-delegation rewrite:
#   The hunk REPLACES the line
#       d = yield* ble() ? oZo(e, t, o) : Oer(e, t, o);
#   Every identifier on it is a bundler name that churns:
#       2.1.260:  Rae / Y4o / I6n  and the array local `n`
#       2.1.263:  ble / oZo / Oer  and the array local `t`
#   A REPLACED line is matched content, so it must be reproduced exactly.
#   There is no anchored alias for any of the three functions: they are
#   module-local generator helpers with no export and no landed anchor name
#   (checked against _renames.json for services/compact/precomputedCompact.js).
#   Rewriting the site to go through a stable global would change evaluation
#   order inside a generator's try/finally — not a safe blind edit.
#
#   Hunk 1 (cli/structuredIO.js) is ALSO version-locked, but only weakly: its
#   context line is `prependUserMessage(t)` — the METHOD name is anchored and
#   stable, only the PARAMETER renamed (`n` on .260, `t` on .263). The class
#   `StructuredIO` IS a landed anchor and appears in the hunk header.
#
# ⛔ WHAT WOULD UNBLOCK IT: an anchor rule naming the three generator helpers
#   (the `Rae`/`ble` pair especially — it is the "is precompute enabled"
#   predicate). With those three named, hunk 2 becomes version-independent.
#
# NO MINIFIED NAME IS INTRODUCED ON AN ADDED LINE that is not also pinned by
# the replaced line itself, which is inside the hunk — so drift FAILS LOUDLY.
#
#
# 🔴 REGENERATED 2026-09-07 — ANCHOR-DRIVEN. Every identifier in both hunks is
#   now an anchored name: query / isObserverAgentsEnabled / queryWithObserverTap
#   / queryLoop / params / consumedCommandUuids, plus the class method
#   prependUserMessage (a method name, which minifiers preserve). NO minified
#   identifier appears on any ADDED line.
#   The manual-iteration shape is preserved deliberately: an earlier
#   for-await rewrite BROKE the generator protocol and lost the loop's return
#   value, which the reason switch downstream reads.
#   Re-derived from the real tree rather than token-swapped — on 008 a pure
#   token swap produced correct names in an unmatchable hunk, because the
#   longer names made prettier reflow the call across three lines.
#
#
# ============================================================================
# 2026-09-20 — AUXILIARY QUERIES WERE BEING MIRRORED AS CONVERSATION
# ============================================================================
# REPORTED: claudiverse showed watcher-2 saying "status?" and "what is filling
#   up the db?" — lines that exist nowhere in its local JSONL transcript.
#
# CAUSE: query() is not only the conversation. Claude Code forks it for
#   internal side-requests — prompt suggestion, session title, memory
#   extraction, away summary, narration, ~25 querySource values — each run
#   with skipTranscript so it never reaches the local JSONL. The mirror hook
#   in query() saw every one of them. The prompt-suggestion fork is the one
#   that made it visible: its system prompt asks the model to predict what the
#   OPERATOR would type next, so its output reads as a user line, and the panel
#   rendered it as an assistant bubble. Measured: three per replay window on
#   watcher-2, message ids absent locally, 1 output token over 763k cached
#   input each.
#
# FIX: mirror only main and subagent sources. The split is upstream's own —
#   coreSchemas ji(): repl_main_thread*/sdk -> main, agent:*/hook_agent ->
#   subagent, undefined -> main, anything else auxiliary. Reproduced inline
#   with string tests on `params.querySource` (both real names: `params` is
#   query()'s own parameter, in the hunk context) so the added lines carry no
#   minified identifier. turn_complete is gated the same way, so a finished
#   side-query cannot look like a finished turn to an orchestrator.
#
# ⚠️ WHAT THIS CHANGES DOWNSTREAM: the Room's idle/busy and note_model no
#   longer see auxiliary traffic. That is the intended direction — a title
#   generation is not the seat being busy — but the idle debounce (patch 008)
#   and any client that counted on those extra frames will see fewer.

